> But not capitalised, IIRC?

Nope. Imprimis, what Boudewijn says is only partly true: some
dictionaries sort ij under i, between ii and ik; some sort it as a
separate letter, after or before the y; and some, in particular
crossword dictionaries, sort it as identical to y. There are historical
reasons for this mess. In any case, ij is capitalised IJ, not Ij. At
least one version of MS Word, even the Dutch edition, is confused by
this; for once, I don't entirely blame Microsoft, since it confuses even
some humans.

